IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`

-- bgg3-civil: BGG 1. Abschnitt, Beschwerde in Zivilsachen (Art. 72 to 77).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
--
-- Every decision function here answers a MAYBE BOOLEAN:
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes to the case, in its own words;
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no to the case, in its own words
--               (a branch tagged  FALSE-kind  names the words);
--   NOTHING     not covered (a branch tagged  NOTHING-kind  says why).
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- The English identifiers are glosses of the German; the quoted lines are the text.

§ `Art 72 Grundsatz (basic rule)`

-- src:11 | 1 Das Bundesgericht beurteilt Beschwerden gegen Entscheide in Zivilsachen.
@ref Art. 72(1) BGG (src:11)
GIVEN `the decision is in a civil matter` IS A BOOLEAN              -- Zivilsache: not defined in this chapter, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(1) the appeal in civil matters lies against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is in a civil matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection reaches only "Entscheide in Zivilsachen" and says nothing of other decisions

-- src:12 | 2 Der Beschwerde in Zivilsachen unterliegen auch:
-- src:13 | a. Entscheide in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen;
@ref Art. 72(2)(a) BGG (src:12-13)
GIVEN `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(a) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the decision in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` MEANS
    IF `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (a) reaches only "Entscheide in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen"

-- Art 72(2)(b), items 1 to 6: "insbesondere Entscheide" -- the text lists examples of
-- public-law decisions in immediate connection with civil law, and does not close the list.
-- Each item answers JUST TRUE for a public-law decision of its kind, and otherwise NOTHING
-- (NOTHING-kind (includes)).  Item 7 is repealed (see the coverage table in NOTES.md).

-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
-- src:15 | 1. über die Anerkennung und Vollstreckung von Entscheiden und über die Rechtshilfe in Zivilsachen,
@ref Art. 72(2)(b)(1) BGG (src:14-15)
GIVEN `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN          -- öffentlich-rechtlicher Entscheid
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(b)(1) the public-law decision on recognition, enforcement or legal assistance is one in immediate connection with civil law` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a public-law decision` AND kind EQUALS `recognition and enforcement of judgments, or legal assistance in civil matters`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples; a decision outside item 1 is not thereby shown to be outside Art 72(2)(b)

-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
-- src:16 | 2. über die Führung des Grundbuchs, des Zivilstands- und des Handelsregisters sowie der Register für Marken, Muster und Modelle, Erfindungspatente, Pflanzensorten und Topografien,
@ref Art. 72(2)(b)(2) BGG (src:14) (src:16)
GIVEN `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(b)(2) the public-law decision on keeping a register is one in immediate connection with civil law` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a public-law decision` AND kind EQUALS `keeping of a land, civil status, commercial or intellectual-property register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
-- src:17 | 3. über die Bewilligung zur Namensänderung,
@ref Art. 72(2)(b)(3) BGG (src:14) (src:17)
GIVEN `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(b)(3) the public-law decision on a name change is one in immediate connection with civil law` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a public-law decision` AND kind EQUALS `permission to change a name`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
-- src:18 | 4. auf dem Gebiet der Aufsicht über die Stiftungen mit Ausnahme der Vorsorge- und Freizügigkeitseinrichtungen,
@ref Art. 72(2)(b)(4) BGG (src:14) (src:18)
GIVEN `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
      `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution` IS A BOOLEAN   -- Vorsorge- und Freizügigkeitseinrichtung
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(b)(4) the public-law decision on supervising a foundation is one in immediate connection with civil law` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a public-law decision` AND kind EQUALS `supervision of foundations` AND (NOT `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "mit Ausnahme der Vorsorge- und Freizügigkeitseinrichtungen"; and (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
-- src:19 | 5.[^1] auf dem Gebiet der Aufsicht über die Willensvollstrecker und ‑vollstreckerinnen und andere erbrechtliche Vertreter und Vertreterinnen,
@ref Art. 72(2)(b)(5) BGG (src:14) (src:19)
GIVEN `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(b)(5) the public-law decision on supervising an executor or succession-law representative is one in immediate connection with civil law` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a public-law decision` AND kind EQUALS `supervision of executors and other succession-law representatives`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
-- src:20 | 6.[^2] auf dem Gebiet des Kindes- und Erwachsenenschutzes,
@ref Art. 72(2)(b)(6) BGG (src:14) (src:20)
GIVEN `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(b)(6) the public-law decision on child and adult protection is one in immediate connection with civil law` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a public-law decision` AND kind EQUALS `child and adult protection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "insbesondere" lists examples

-- Item 7 ("7.[^3] …", repealed by footnote 3): nothing to encode.

-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
@ref Art. 72(2)(b) BGG (src:14)
GIVEN `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` IS A BOOLEAN    -- "in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht": a judgment the text leaves open, taken as an input
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
      `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2)(b) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the public-law decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision is a public-law decision` AND (`the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` OR `a listed item applies`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (b) reaches only public-law decisions "die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen" (the "insbesondere" items are examples, not the whole of the test: fork F1)
    WHERE
        `a listed item applies` MEANS
                fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(b)(1) the public-law decision on recognition, enforcement or legal assistance is one in immediate connection with civil law` `the decision is a public-law decision` kind)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(b)(2) the public-law decision on keeping a register is one in immediate connection with civil law` `the decision is a public-law decision` kind)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(b)(3) the public-law decision on a name change is one in immediate connection with civil law` `the decision is a public-law decision` kind)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(b)(4) the public-law decision on supervising a foundation is one in immediate connection with civil law` `the decision is a public-law decision` kind `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution`)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(b)(5) the public-law decision on supervising an executor or succession-law representative is one in immediate connection with civil law` `the decision is a public-law decision` kind)
            OR  fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(b)(6) the public-law decision on child and adult protection is one in immediate connection with civil law` `the decision is a public-law decision` kind)

-- src:12 | 2 Der Beschwerde in Zivilsachen unterliegen auch:
-- src:13 | a. Entscheide in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen;
-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
@ref Art. 72(2) BGG (src:12-14)
GIVEN `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
      `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72(2) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the decision` MEANS
    IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(a) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the decision in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2)(b) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the public-law decision` `the decision is a public-law decision` `the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` kind `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unterliegen auch" names items (a) and (b) and does not say no to a decision outside them

-- src:11 | 1 Das Bundesgericht beurteilt Beschwerden gegen Entscheide in Zivilsachen.
-- src:12 | 2 Der Beschwerde in Zivilsachen unterliegen auch:
-- src:13 | a. Entscheide in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen;
-- src:14 | b. öffentlich-rechtliche Entscheide, die in unmittelbarem Zusammenhang mit Zivilrecht stehen, insbesondere Entscheide:
@ref Art. 72 BGG (src:11-14)
GIVEN `the decision is in a civil matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a public-law decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of public-law decision listed in Art 72(2)(b)`
      `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 72 the appeal in civil matters lies against the decision` MEANS
    IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(1) the appeal in civil matters lies against the decision` `the decision is in a civil matter`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 72(2) the appeal in civil matters also lies against the decision` `the decision is in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` `the decision is a public-law decision` `the decision stands in immediate connection with civil law` kind `the foundation is a pension or vested-benefits institution`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): Art 72 states what the appeal in civil matters reaches and does not say no to anything else

§ `Art 73 Ausnahme (exception)`

-- src:24 | Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide, die im Rahmen des Widerspruchsverfahrens gegen eine Marke getroffen worden sind.
@ref Art. 73 BGG (src:24)
GIVEN `the decision was made in opposition proceedings against a trade mark` IS A BOOLEAN    -- Widerspruchsverfahren gegen eine Marke
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 73 the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision` MEANS
    IF `the decision was made in opposition proceedings against a trade mark`
    THEN JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Die Beschwerde ist unzulässig gegen Entscheide, die im Rahmen des Widerspruchsverfahrens gegen eine Marke getroffen worden sind."
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar reaches only trade mark opposition decisions; it does not say that any other decision is admissible

§ `Art 74 Streitwertgrenze (value threshold)`

-- src:27 | 1 In vermögensrechtlichen Angelegenheiten ist die Beschwerde nur zulässig, wenn der Streitwert mindestens beträgt:
-- src:28 | a. 15 000 Franken in arbeits- und mietrechtlichen Fällen;
@ref Art. 74(1)(a) BGG (src:27-28)
GIVEN `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN               -- vermögensrechtliche Angelegenheit
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN             -- arbeitsrechtlicher Fall
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN                 -- mietrechtlicher Fall
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER                  -- Streitwert: how it is worked out is outside this chapter
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(1)(a) the value in dispute is enough in an employment or tenancy law case` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the matter is a pecuniary matter` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In vermögensrechtlichen Angelegenheiten"; a non-pecuniary matter is outside the subsection
        IF NOT (`the case is an employment law case` OR `the case is a tenancy law case`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (a) covers only "arbeits- und mietrechtlichen Fällen"
        IF `the value in dispute in francs` AT LEAST 15000 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist die Beschwerde nur zulässig, wenn der Streitwert mindestens beträgt"

-- src:27 | 1 In vermögensrechtlichen Angelegenheiten ist die Beschwerde nur zulässig, wenn der Streitwert mindestens beträgt:
-- src:29 | b. 30 000 Franken in allen übrigen Fällen.
@ref Art. 74(1)(b) BGG (src:27) (src:29)
GIVEN `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(1)(b) the value in dispute is enough in all other cases` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the matter is a pecuniary matter` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In vermögensrechtlichen Angelegenheiten"
        IF `the case is an employment law case` OR `the case is a tenancy law case` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (b) covers only "allen übrigen Fällen"; item (a) governs employment and tenancy law cases
        IF `the value in dispute in francs` AT LEAST 30000 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist die Beschwerde nur zulässig, wenn der Streitwert mindestens beträgt"

-- src:27 | 1 In vermögensrechtlichen Angelegenheiten ist die Beschwerde nur zulässig, wenn der Streitwert mindestens beträgt:
-- src:28 | a. 15 000 Franken in arbeits- und mietrechtlichen Fällen;
-- src:29 | b. 30 000 Franken in allen übrigen Fällen.
@ref Art. 74(1) BGG (src:27-29)
GIVEN `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(1) the value in dispute is enough` MEANS
    IF `the case is an employment law case` OR `the case is a tenancy law case`
    THEN `Art 74(1)(a) the value in dispute is enough in an employment or tenancy law case` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `the value in dispute in francs`
    ELSE `Art 74(1)(b) the value in dispute is enough in all other cases` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `the value in dispute in francs`

-- Art 74(2): "Erreicht der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht, so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:" is followed by five limbs.
-- Limbs (a) and (b) open with "wenn": a failed "wenn" counts as the text's no (the rule of 2026-10-29, reading (a), for a lawyer).
-- Limbs (c) to (e) say "gegen Entscheide der ...": outside the named decisions the answer is NOTHING.

-- src:30 | 2 Erreicht der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht, so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:
-- src:31 | a. wenn sich eine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt;
@ref Art. 74(2)(a) BGG (src:30-31)
GIVEN `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS A BOOLEAN       -- Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung: an open-textured judgment, asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2)(a) the appeal is admissible although the value is short, because a legal question of fundamental importance arises` MEANS
    IF `a legal question of fundamental importance arises`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn sich eine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt" (a failed "wenn")

-- src:30 | 2 Erreicht der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht, so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:
-- src:32 | b.[^4] wenn ein Bundesgesetz eine einzige kantonale Instanz vorsieht;
@ref Art. 74(2)(b) BGG (src:30) (src:32)
GIVEN `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2)(b) the appeal is admissible although the value is short, because a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` MEANS
    IF `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn ein Bundesgesetz eine einzige kantonale Instanz vorsieht" (a failed "wenn")

-- src:30 | 2 Erreicht der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht, so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:
-- src:33 | c. gegen Entscheide der kantonalen Aufsichtsbehörden in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen;
@ref Art. 74(2)(c) BGG (src:30) (src:33)
GIVEN `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN    -- kantonale Aufsichtsbehörde in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2)(c) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority` MEANS
    IF `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (c) names only "Entscheide der kantonalen Aufsichtsbehörden in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen"

-- src:30 | 2 Erreicht der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht, so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:
-- src:34 | d. gegen Entscheide des Konkurs- und Nachlassrichters oder der Konkurs- und Nachlassrichterin;
@ref Art. 74(2)(d) BGG (src:30) (src:34)
GIVEN `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` IS A BOOLEAN      -- Konkurs- und Nachlassrichter
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2)(d) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of the bankruptcy and composition judge` MEANS
    IF `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (d) names only "Entscheide des Konkurs- und Nachlassrichters"

-- src:30 | 2 Erreicht der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht, so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:
-- src:35 | e.[^5] gegen Entscheide des Bundespatentgerichts.
@ref Art. 74(2)(e) BGG (src:30) (src:35)
GIVEN body IS A `Deciding body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2)(e) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of the Federal Patent Court` MEANS
    IF body EQUALS `Federal Patent Court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): item (e) names only "Entscheide des Bundespatentgerichts"

-- src:30 | 2 Erreicht der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht, so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:
-- src:31 | a. wenn sich eine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt;
-- src:32 | b.[^4] wenn ein Bundesgesetz eine einzige kantonale Instanz vorsieht;
-- src:33 | c. gegen Entscheide der kantonalen Aufsichtsbehörden in Schuldbetreibungs- und Konkurssachen;
-- src:34 | d. gegen Entscheide des Konkurs- und Nachlassrichters oder der Konkurs- und Nachlassrichterin;
-- src:35 | e.[^5] gegen Entscheide des Bundespatentgerichts.
@ref Art. 74(2) BGG (src:30-35)
GIVEN `the matter is a pecuniary matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is an employment law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the case is a tenancy law case` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER
      `a legal question of fundamental importance arises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge` IS A BOOLEAN
      body IS A `Deciding body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 74(2) the appeal is admissible although the value is short` MEANS
    IF `Art 74(1) the value in dispute is enough` `the matter is a pecuniary matter` `the case is an employment law case` `the case is a tenancy law case` `the value in dispute in francs` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN
        IF       fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(a) the appeal is admissible although the value is short, because a legal question of fundamental importance arises` `a legal question of fundamental importance arises`)
              OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(b) the appeal is admissible although the value is short, because a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance`)
              OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(c) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of a cantonal supervisory authority` `the decision is of a cantonal supervisory authority in a debt enforcement or bankruptcy matter`)
              OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(d) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of the bankruptcy and composition judge` `the decision is of the bankruptcy and composition judge`)
              OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 74(2)(e) the appeal is admissible although the value is short against a decision of the Federal Patent Court` body)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so ist die Beschwerde dennoch zulässig:" and no limb holds; this subsection gives no saving on these facts (the provision's own question, in the manner of a defence: marginal reading for a lawyer; fork F2)
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies only where "der Streitwert den massgebenden Betrag nach Absatz 1 nicht" erreicht

§ `Art 75 Vorinstanzen (lower instances)`

-- src:38 | 1 Die Beschwerde ist zulässig gegen Entscheide letzter kantonaler Instanzen, des Bundesverwaltungsgerichts und des Bundespatentgerichts.[^6]
@ref Art. 75(1) BGG (src:38)
GIVEN body IS A `Deciding body`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the decision of this body` MEANS
    CONSIDER body
    WHEN `last cantonal instance` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Federal Administrative Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Federal Patent Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING       -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "zulässig gegen Entscheide letzter kantonaler Instanzen, des Bundesverwaltungsgerichts und des Bundespatentgerichts" names three bodies and does not close the list with "nur"

-- src:39 | 2 Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein. Diese entscheiden als Rechtsmittelinstanzen; ausgenommen sind die Fälle, in denen:
-- src:40 | a.[^7] ein Bundesgesetz eine einzige kantonale Instanz vorsieht;
@ref Art. 75(2)(a) BGG (src:39-40)
GIVEN `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(2)(a) the exception applies, because a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` MEANS
    IF `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception reaches only "die Fälle, in denen" a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance

-- src:39 | 2 Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein. Diese entscheiden als Rechtsmittelinstanzen; ausgenommen sind die Fälle, in denen:
-- src:41 | b. ein Fachgericht für handelsrechtliche Streitigkeiten als einzige kantonale Instanz entscheidet;
@ref Art. 75(2)(b) BGG (src:39) (src:41)
GIVEN `a specialised commercial court decided as the single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN    -- Fachgericht für handelsrechtliche Streitigkeiten
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(2)(b) the exception applies, because a specialised commercial court decided as the single cantonal instance` MEANS
    IF `a specialised commercial court decided as the single cantonal instance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception reaches only "die Fälle, in denen" a specialised commercial court decides as the single cantonal instance

-- src:39 | 2 Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein. Diese entscheiden als Rechtsmittelinstanzen; ausgenommen sind die Fälle, in denen:
-- src:42 | c.[^8] eine Klage mit einem Streitwert von mindestens 100 000 Franken mit Zustimmung aller Parteien direkt beim oberen Gericht eingereicht wurde.
@ref Art. 75(2)(c) BGG (src:39) (src:42)
GIVEN `the action was filed directly with the upper court with the consent of all parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(2)(c) the exception applies, because an action of at least 100000 francs was filed directly with the upper court` MEANS
    IF `the action was filed directly with the upper court with the consent of all parties` AND `the value in dispute in francs` AT LEAST 100000
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the exception reaches only an action "mit einem Streitwert von mindestens 100 000 Franken mit Zustimmung aller Parteien direkt beim oberen Gericht eingereicht"

-- src:39 | 2 Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein. Diese entscheiden als Rechtsmittelinstanzen; ausgenommen sind die Fälle, in denen:
-- src:40 | a.[^7] ein Bundesgesetz eine einzige kantonale Instanz vorsieht;
-- src:41 | b. ein Fachgericht für handelsrechtliche Streitigkeiten als einzige kantonale Instanz entscheidet;
-- src:42 | c.[^8] eine Klage mit einem Streitwert von mindestens 100 000 Franken mit Zustimmung aller Parteien direkt beim oberen Gericht eingereicht wurde.
@ref Art. 75(2) BGG (src:39-42)
GIVEN `the last cantonal instance is an upper court` IS A BOOLEAN                        -- oberes Gericht
      `the last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance` IS A BOOLEAN            -- als Rechtsmittelinstanz
      `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a specialised commercial court decided as the single cantonal instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action was filed directly with the upper court with the consent of all parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value in dispute in francs` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 75(2) the last cantonal instance is an upper court deciding as an appeal instance, or an exception applies` MEANS
    IF     (`the last cantonal instance is an upper court` AND `the last cantonal instance decided as an appeal instance`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 75(2)(a) the exception applies, because a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance` `a federal statute provides for a single cantonal instance`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 75(2)(b) the exception applies, because a specialised commercial court decided as the single cantonal instance` `a specialised commercial court decided as the single cantonal instance`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 75(2)(c) the exception applies, because an action of at least 100000 francs was filed directly with the upper court` `the action was filed directly with the upper court with the consent of all parties` `the value in dispute in francs`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a duty on the cantons ("Die Kantone setzen ... ein"); the text states no consequence for the person if a canton did not comply (a bare must not done: fork F5)

-- The cantons' duty in Art 75(2), as a regulative rule.  No time limit is stated and none is invented.
-- src:39 | 2 Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein. Diese entscheiden als Rechtsmittelinstanzen; ausgenommen sind die Fälle, in denen:
@ref Art. 75(2) BGG (the duty) (src:39)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Actor in chapter 3` `Cantonal act in chapter 3`
`Art 75(2) the cantons' duty to set up an upper court as last cantonal instance` MEANS
    PARTY Canton
    MUST `set up an upper court as last cantonal instance, deciding as an appeal instance`

§ `Art 76 Beschwerderecht (standing)`

-- src:45 | 1 Zur Beschwerde in Zivilsachen ist berechtigt, wer:
-- src:46 | a. vor der Vorinstanz am Verfahren teilgenommen hat oder keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten hat; und
@ref Art. 76(1)(a) BGG (src:45-46)
GIVEN `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN       -- am Verfahren teilgenommen
      `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN         -- keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(1)(a) the person took part before the lower instance or had no chance to` MEANS
    IF `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` OR `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist berechtigt, wer: a. vor der Vorinstanz am Verfahren teilgenommen hat oder keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten hat" (a failed condition of an entitlement: reading (a), for a lawyer)

-- src:45 | 1 Zur Beschwerde in Zivilsachen ist berechtigt, wer:
-- src:47 | b.[^9] durch den angefochtenen Entscheid besonders berührt ist und ein schutzwürdiges Interesse an dessen Aufhebung oder Änderung hat.
@ref Art. 76(1)(b) BGG (src:45) (src:47)
GIVEN `the person is especially affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN                         -- besonders berührt
      `the person has an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN -- schutzwürdiges Interesse
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(1)(b) the person is especially affected and has an interest worthy of protection` MEANS
    IF `the person is especially affected by the decision` AND `the person has an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "ist berechtigt, wer: ... durch den angefochtenen Entscheid besonders berührt ist und ein schutzwürdiges Interesse an dessen Aufhebung oder Änderung hat" (a failed condition of an entitlement: reading (a), for a lawyer)

-- src:45 | 1 Zur Beschwerde in Zivilsachen ist berechtigt, wer:
-- src:46 | a. vor der Vorinstanz am Verfahren teilgenommen hat oder keine Möglichkeit zur Teilnahme erhalten hat; und
-- src:47 | b.[^9] durch den angefochtenen Entscheid besonders berührt ist und ein schutzwürdiges Interesse an dessen Aufhebung oder Änderung hat.
@ref Art. 76(1) BGG (src:45-47)
GIVEN `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is especially affected by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(1) the person is entitled to appeal in civil matters` MEANS
    IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 76(1)(a) the person took part before the lower instance or had no chance to` `the person took part in the proceedings before the lower instance` `the person had no chance to take part before the lower instance`)
       AND fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 76(1)(b) the person is especially affected and has an interest worthy of protection` `the person is especially affected by the decision` `the person has an interest worthy of protection in its quashing or change`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Zur Beschwerde in Zivilsachen ist berechtigt, wer: a. ...; und b. ..." (an entitled-named function: fork F3; Art 76(2) gives other bodies standing, so this answers only the provision's own question)

-- src:48 | 2 Gegen Entscheide nach Artikel 72 Absatz 2 steht das Beschwerderecht auch der Bundeskanzlei, den Departementen des Bundes oder, soweit das Bundesrecht es vorsieht, den ihnen unterstellten Dienststellen zu, wenn der angefochtene Entscheid die Bundesgesetzgebung in ihrem Aufgabenbereich verletzen kann.[^10]
@ref Art. 76(2) BGG (src:48)
GIVEN `the decision is one under Art 72(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appellant is the Federal Chancellery or a federal department` IS A BOOLEAN              -- Bundeskanzlei, Departemente des Bundes
      `the appellant is a subordinate service and federal law provides for its right` IS A BOOLEAN   -- "soweit das Bundesrecht es vorsieht, den ihnen unterstellten Dienststellen"
      `the decision can violate federal legislation in the appellant's field` IS A BOOLEAN         -- Verletzung der Bundesgesetzgebung im Aufgabenbereich
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 76(2) the federal authority is also entitled to appeal in civil matters` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the decision is one under Art 72(2)` THEN NOTHING     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Gegen Entscheide nach Artikel 72 Absatz 2"
        IF NOT (`the appellant is the Federal Chancellery or a federal department` OR `the appellant is a subordinate service and federal law provides for its right`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "der Bundeskanzlei, den Departementen des Bundes oder, soweit das Bundesrecht es vorsieht, den ihnen unterstellten Dienststellen"
        IF `the decision can violate federal legislation in the appellant's field` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "wenn der angefochtene Entscheid die Bundesgesetzgebung in ihrem Aufgabenbereich verletzen kann" (a failed "wenn" on an entitlement: fork F3)

§ `Art 77 Schiedsgerichtsbarkeit (arbitration)`

-- src:51 | 1 Die Beschwerde in Zivilsachen ist ungeachtet des Streitwerts zulässig gegen Entscheide von Schiedsgerichten:[^12]
-- src:52 | a. in der internationalen Schiedsgerichtsbarkeit unter den Voraussetzungen der Artikel 190–192 des Bundesgesetzes vom 18. Dezember 1987[^13] über das Internationale Privatrecht;
@ref Art. 77(1)(a) BGG (src:51-52)
GIVEN `the decision is of an arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN                                -- Entscheid eines Schiedsgerichts
      `the arbitration is international` IS A BOOLEAN                                        -- internationale Schiedsgerichtsbarkeit
      `the conditions of Arts 190 to 192 of the Private International Law Act are met` IS A BOOLEAN   -- IPRG (SR 291), outside the sources: asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1)(a) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the international arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` MEANS
    IF `the decision is of an arbitral tribunal` AND `the arbitration is international` AND `the conditions of Arts 190 to 192 of the Private International Law Act are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unter den Voraussetzungen der Artikel 190–192" of another Act, outside the sources (points outside the text; fork F14)

-- src:51 | 1 Die Beschwerde in Zivilsachen ist ungeachtet des Streitwerts zulässig gegen Entscheide von Schiedsgerichten:[^12]
-- src:53 | b. in der nationalen Schiedsgerichtsbarkeit unter den Voraussetzungen der Artikel 389–395 der Zivilprozessordnung vom 19. Dezember 2008[^14].[^15]
@ref Art. 77(1)(b) BGG (src:51) (src:53)
GIVEN `the decision is of an arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arbitration is national` IS A BOOLEAN                                             -- nationale Schiedsgerichtsbarkeit
      `the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 of the Civil Procedure Code are met` IS A BOOLEAN   -- ZPO (SR 272), outside the sources: asked as a fact
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1)(b) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the national arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` MEANS
    IF `the decision is of an arbitral tribunal` AND `the arbitration is national` AND `the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 of the Civil Procedure Code are met`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unter den Voraussetzungen der Artikel 389–395" of another Act, outside the sources (points outside the text; fork F14)

-- src:51 | 1 Die Beschwerde in Zivilsachen ist ungeachtet des Streitwerts zulässig gegen Entscheide von Schiedsgerichten:[^12]
-- src:52 | a. in der internationalen Schiedsgerichtsbarkeit unter den Voraussetzungen der Artikel 190–192 des Bundesgesetzes vom 18. Dezember 1987[^13] über das Internationale Privatrecht;
-- src:53 | b. in der nationalen Schiedsgerichtsbarkeit unter den Voraussetzungen der Artikel 389–395 der Zivilprozessordnung vom 19. Dezember 2008[^14].[^15]
@ref Art. 77(1) BGG (src:51-53)
GIVEN `the decision is of an arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arbitration is international` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arbitration is national` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of Arts 190 to 192 of the Private International Law Act are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 of the Civil Procedure Code are met` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(1) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` MEANS
    IF     fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 77(1)(a) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the international arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` `the decision is of an arbitral tribunal` `the arbitration is international` `the conditions of Arts 190 to 192 of the Private International Law Act are met`)
        OR fromMaybe FALSE (`Art 77(1)(b) the appeal in civil matters is admissible against the national arbitral award whatever the value in dispute` `the decision is of an arbitral tribunal` `the arbitration is national` `the conditions of Arts 389 to 395 of the Civil Procedure Code are met`)
    THEN JUST TRUE          -- "ungeachtet des Streitwerts": the value in dispute (Art 74) plays no part in this answer
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "unter den Voraussetzungen" of Arts 190-192 IPRG or 389-395 ZPO (points outside the text)

-- src:54 | 2 Die Artikel 48 Absatz 3, 90–98, 103 Absatz 2, 105 Absatz 2, 106 Absatz 1 sowie 107 Absatz 2, soweit dieser dem Bundesgericht erlaubt, in der Sache selbst zu entscheiden, sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar.[^16]
@ref Art. 77(2) BGG (src:54)
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      article IS A NUMBER                                                                   -- the number of the provision of the Act asked about
      paragraph IS A NUMBER                                                                 -- its paragraph; 0 asks about the whole Article
      `the provision is used to let the Court decide the matter itself` IS A BOOLEAN        -- only for Art 107(2): "soweit dieser dem Bundesgericht erlaubt, in der Sache selbst zu entscheiden"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(2) the listed provision is applicable to the appeal against the arbitral award` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in diesen Fällen", the appeals of Art 77(1)
        IF article EQUALS 48 AND paragraph EQUALS 3 THEN JUST FALSE            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Die Artikel 48 Absatz 3 ... sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar."
        IF article AT LEAST 90 AND article AT MOST 98 THEN JUST FALSE          -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "90–98 ... sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar"
        IF article EQUALS 103 AND paragraph EQUALS 2 THEN JUST FALSE           -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "103 Absatz 2 ... sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar."
        IF article EQUALS 105 AND paragraph EQUALS 2 THEN JUST FALSE           -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "105 Absatz 2 ... sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar."
        IF article EQUALS 106 AND paragraph EQUALS 1 THEN JUST FALSE           -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "106 Absatz 1 ... sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar."
        IF article EQUALS 107 AND paragraph EQUALS 2 AND `the provision is used to let the Court decide the matter itself` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "sowie 107 Absatz 2, soweit dieser dem Bundesgericht erlaubt, in der Sache selbst zu entscheiden, sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar."
        OTHERWISE NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): a provision the paragraph does not name is not said to be inapplicable (nor applicable); and for Art 107(2) outside "soweit dieser dem Bundesgericht erlaubt, in der Sache selbst zu entscheiden" (limited by its own wording)

-- src:55 | 2bis Rechtsschriften können in englischer Sprache abgefasst werden.[^17]
@ref Art. 77(2bis) BGG (src:55)
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(2bis) the written submission may be drafted in English` MEANS
    IF `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph stands in Art 77 (arbitration); whether it reaches other appeals the sentence does not say (fork F6)

-- src:56 | 3 Das Bundesgericht prüft nur Rügen, die in der Beschwerde vorgebracht und begründet worden sind.
@ref Art. 77(3) BGG (src:56)
GIVEN `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the complaint was raised in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN                                 -- vorgebracht
      `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN                               -- begründet
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 77(3) the complaint meets the condition for being examined` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the appeal is against an arbitral award under Art 77(1)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph stands in Art 77 (arbitration); fork F6
        IF `the complaint was raised in the appeal` AND `the complaint was reasoned in the appeal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE     -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Das Bundesgericht prüft nur Rügen, die in der Beschwerde vorgebracht und begründet worden sind."
